## Key Findings

During testing, several issues were identified across the application.

The main findings included:

* Deleted Board items remained visible after deletion and refresh.
* Draft content was not preserved after page refresh.
* Draft initially failed to load correctly in some cases.
* Draft Editor entered lowercase text as uppercase.
* AI Assistant was unable to reliably create or write content into an editable Draft.
* A new Draft could retain context from a previous independent conversation.
* AI-generated Plan content was not reflected on the Plan page.
* Poster changes were not applied immediately after saving.
* The poster upload dialog could display a previously uploaded image instead of the current poster.
* New Chat could temporarily display the previous conversation.
* Pagination/page breaks were duplicated or reset when the same Draft was opened in Split View.

---

## UX Recommendations

In addition to functional bugs, usability improvements were identified.

Examples include:

* Adding a visible Close (X) button to the Project / Manuscript details panel.
* Adding a grab/hand cursor to draggable Template elements.

These items were documented separately from functional defects because the current functionality still works, but the user experience could be clearer.

